# The shop-board Vercel project deploys the root static site + api/ + shared/.
# This file is honoured by the GIT-INTEGRATION deploys too, not just the CLI
# (verified 2026-09-17: `migrations/*.sql` is git-tracked AND listed below and
# returns 404 on www + test.*, while the git-tracked, NOT-listed
# `staging/staging-rls-and-storage.sql` returns 200). So a line here is the way
# to keep a TRACKED file off the public origin, not only untracked cruft.

# kiki/ is a SEPARATE Next.js project with its own deployment — not part of
# shop-board. Its build cache + bundled manual PDF blow past Vercel's 100 MB
# per-file upload limit.
kiki

# Dependencies + build caches — Vercel installs from package.json at build time.
node_modules
.next

# Local test data + OS junk.
parking-test-20.csv
*.DS_Store
.DS_Store

# ── Internal working documents — NOT app content (added 2026-08-19) ────────
# A CLI `vercel --prod` uploads the working tree, so without these lines each
# of these was served publicly on prod (verified http 200 on the live domain).
# No credential VALUES were exposed — only internal notes — but none of this is
# app content. Verified 2026-08-19: no reference to any of these names exists in
# api/, shared/, *.html, *.css or vercel.json.
SESSION_HANDOFF_2026-07-29.md
SESSION_HANDOFF_2026-07-30.md
SESSION_HANDOFF_*.md
lee_transmission_shop_board_session_memory.txt
lee-transmission-marketplace-model.md
setup_shopboard.sql
shop-lot-map.svg
.claude

# migrations/ — hand-run SQL, applied by a human in the Supabase SQL editor.
# Verified 2026-08-19 that NOTHING reads these at runtime: every occurrence of
# "migrations/" in api/ and shared/ is a comment or an error-message string,
# there is no fetch/readFile/require/import of a .sql file anywhere in served
# code, and vercel.json neither routes nor includes them.
migrations

# ── Tracked but NOT public (added 2026-09-17) ──────────────────────────────
# The office-auth wiring doc describes the auth design in detail; it stays in git
# for developers but must not be served. It is also removed from the File Cabinet
# manifest (shared/file-cabinet.js) — pulling it from the manifest alone would
# NOT remove its URL. No runtime code fetches it (only comments name it).
docs/wiring/office-auth.md

# scripts/ — operator tools run from a laptop (scripts/meta-sim.mjs signs fake Meta
# deliveries for test.*). Not app content; nothing served reads them. (2026-09-23)
scripts

# CLAUDE.md — the Claude Code project instructions. Internal (project ids, deploy
# process, security design); it was publicly readable at /CLAUDE.md until
# 2026-09-23. Stays in git; nothing served reads it. (Cris, 2026-09-23)
CLAUDE.md
